# Staging before production (mandatory)

Ship to **staging** by default. **Production** only when the user explicitly asks (e.g. “push to production”, “ship to prod”, “promote to live”).

## Stacks

| | Staging (default) | Production (user request only) |
|---|---|---|
| Env | `.env.staging` | `.env` |
| Port | 8081 | 8080 |
| API | `https://api-staging.pokepon.org` | `https://api.pokepon.org` |
| DB | `data/poke_cards_staging.db` | `data/poke_cards.db` |
| Bot deploy | `scripts/start-bot-staging.sh` / `deploy-mac-staging.sh` | `scripts/deploy-mac.sh` |
| Website | **https://staging.pokepon.org** | **https://pokepon.org** |
| Website push | `hamiebrooklyn.github.io` → `bash scripts/deploy-website-staging.sh` | `bash scripts/promote-website-to-production.sh` |

Setup: `docs/STAGING.md` · Website: `hamiebrooklyn.github.io/docs/WEBSITE_STAGING.md`

## Agent workflow (every feature / fix)

1. **Code** in this repo (and `hamiebrooklyn.github.io` if the site UI changes).
2. **Restart staging bot** (mandatory after bot/API changes — you run it in the background; do not ask the user):
   ```bash
   cd ~/Developer/Poke-Cards
   bash scripts/start-bot-staging.sh
   ```
   - Runs `alembic upgrade head`, restarts on `:8081`.
   - Uncommitted bot work: `bash scripts/deploy-mac-staging.sh --no-pull`.
   - **Never** end a bot/API feature turn without restarting staging.
3. **Push to the staging website** when HTML/JS/CSS changed:
   ```bash
   cd ~/Documents/GitHub/hamiebrooklyn.github.io
   git checkout staging
   bash scripts/deploy-website-staging.sh
   ```
4. **Report staging ready** — site **https://staging.pokepon.org**, API on **api-staging**.
5. **Stop** — do not promote to production unless the user asked in that message.

## Why production can pick up staging work (read this)

Production and staging **share one codebase folder** (`~/Developer/Poke-Cards`). The production **launchd** job runs `python -m poke_pon_bot` from that folder — any local file edit is what production loads on its **next restart**.

- **Schema:** `deploy-mac.sh` and the bot’s startup auto-migration run Alembic against **production** `data/poke_cards.db` unless you explicitly source `.env.staging`.
- **Behavior:** New features must be gated until promotion. Notification/inbox code uses `POKEPON_RUNTIME=staging` or `WEB_NOTIFICATIONS_ENABLED=1` (set the latter in `.env` only when the user asks to ship notifications to prod).

**Never** run bare `alembic upgrade head` without sourcing the right env file.

## Push to production (only when the user says so)

**Website** (hamiebrooklyn.github.io):
```bash
bash scripts/promote-website-to-production.sh
```

**Bot** (this repo):
```bash
bash scripts/deploy-mac.sh
```

When promoting notification features, add to production `.env`:
```
WEB_NOTIFICATIONS_ENABLED=1
```
Then run `deploy-mac.sh` (or restart the production launchd job).

## Forbidden without user asking for production

- `deploy-mac.sh` or production bot restart for feature work
- `promote-website-to-production.sh` or `git push origin main` on the website repo
- Claiming the feature is “live on pokepon.org” when only staging was pushed

## Allowed without staging

- Comments, docs-only, no runtime change
- Emergency production hotfix **only** if the user explicitly says skip staging — note what was not tested

## Do not

- Point `.env.staging` at production `DATABASE_URL` or `DISCORD_TOKEN`
- Use `stop-bot.sh` for staging (port 8080 = production only)
- Tell the user to restart the staging bot — use `scripts/start-bot-staging.sh` yourself

## Keep staging running

Prefer the launchd service (survives logout / reboot):

```bash
bash scripts/install-bot-staging-service.sh
```

Or one-off:

```bash
bash scripts/start-bot-staging.sh
```

Tunnel: `api-staging.pokepon.org` → `:8081` in `~/.cloudflared/config.yml`.
